# PROMPT

You extract structured data from scientific articles.

Please read the following paragraphs, find all the nano-composite samples, and fill out the given JSON template for each one of those nanocomposite samples. Do not merge samples of different compositions. If an attribute is not mentioned, fill that section with "null". Mass and Volume Composition should be followed by a %.

# JSON Template:

```txt
{ "Matrix Chemical Name": "matrix_chemical_name", "Matrix Chemical Abbreviation": "matrix_abbreviation", "Filler Chemical Name": "filler_chemical_name", "Filler Chemical Abbreviation": "filler_abbreviation", "Filler Composition Mass": "filler_mass_value", "Filler Composition Volume": "filler_volume_value", "Filler Particle Surface Treatment Chemical Name": "surface_treatment_chemical_name" "Properties": [ { "property name": "property_name", "headers": ["header1", "header2"], "data": [] } ]   
} 
```

Properties is a list of dictionaries where each dictionary represents a property of the nanocomposite. The property name should be filled out with the name of the property where the choicese are: electrical, mechanical, viscoelastic, thermal, volumetric, rheological. The headers should be filled out with the x and y labels which are the names of the conditions or the labels of the data (e.g. time, temperature, frequency, strain, conductivity, dielectric strength, etc.). The data should be a list of (x, y) tuples. For example, if the property is 24 MPa at temperature $25^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ and 30 MPa at temperature $50^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ , the data should be [(25, 24), (50, 30)]. If no data is mentioned, please fill it with null.

